<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Undang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Undang are the four great territorial chiefs of Negeri Sembilan in Malaysia, ruling the districts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sungai-ujong">Sungai Ujong</a>, Jelebu, Johol and Rembau. Under the matrilineal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adat">adat</a> perpatih customs brought by Minangkabau settlers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, they hold the right to choose the state's ruler, the Yang di-Pertuan Besar. The arrangement survives in the state's modern constitution.</p></div>
